From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:54:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a standby is warm before it takes over and its
 recovery yields to requests

A standby (gateway.runtime_lock_wait_seconds) imported only the boot's modules before it waited, so the gateway that took over spent its first seconds importing the turn, API and SDK code its first requests needed, rebuilding the tool schemas, the model context window, the skill index and the HTTP client, and recovering its sessions in one blocking pass on the event loop. On a CPU-starved node that delayed hub events and API answers by many seconds. The owner now records the modules it imported in $HERMES_HOME/cache/gateway_warm_modules.json; a standby imports them before it waits, runs the boot's turn-machinery warm-up, parses the config and every skill's frontmatter (now kept by its text) and builds the OpenAI client once, opening no store and taking no lock. After the lock, local session recovery and the native-session scan run in 20 ms slices with the event loop free between them.
